{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The Rock that begot you, you neglect.</b> It may be explained in the manner of Amram, of blessed memory (Zohar vol. III 287a): at the time the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to create man, He took counsel with the angels, and they said before Him, ״מָה אֱנוֹשׁ״ etc. (Psalms 8:5), and HaShem set Himself against the words of the angels and created him and punished the dissenters — thus far. And therefore, when Israel transgress His will, they weaken the rationale for the creation of man, and this is what the verse says: ״you neglect [the Rock] that begot you.״" "<b>And you forgot El who adorned you.</b> The expression may be understood as an ornament (עֲדִי), in the manner of the verse (Hosea 2:15) ״וַתַּעַד נִזְמָהּ וְחֶלְיָתָהּ,״ and the intention is that He made you an ornament (מָחוֹל, cf. מְחֹלְלֶךָ) — an adornment over all created beings, even over the angels, as it says (Psalms 66:12) ״הִרְכַּבְתָּ אֱנוֹשׁ לְרֹאשֵׁנוּ.״ Or it may be understood in the manner of the verse (Isaiah 49:3) ״יִשְׂרָאֵל אֲשֶׁר בְּךָ אֶתְפָּאָר״ — that He made you an ornament for Him, blessed be He. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Sifrei) homiletical interpretations, such as ״like a hammer״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:29.323529206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}